From: Sirius port
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] ARM: dts: qcom: msm8974: throttle the CPUs at 80 C, as Sony does

The four CPU thermal zones carry a 75 C passive trip inherited from the SoC
tree. With cpufreq cooling bound to them (patch 12) that trip decides how
fast the phone runs under load, and 75 C is reached within seconds of a
single core at 2150 MHz (tsens on a Xperia Z2: 67 -> 78 C in five seconds
under a matrix-multiply load), after which the governor drops the clock by
several steps.

Sony's factory thermal policy for this phone (qcom,msm-thermal in the stock
device tree) throttles at 80 C with 10 C hysteresis, unplugs cores at 85 C
and resets the chip at 115 C. Move the passive trip to 80 C with 5 C
hysteresis. The 110 C critical trip is unchanged and still sits below
Sony's reset point.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8974.dtsi
@@ -2368,8 +2368,8 @@
 
 			trips {
 				cpu_alert0: trip0 {
-					temperature = <75000>;
-					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					temperature = <80000>;
+					hysteresis = <5000>;
 					type = "passive";
 				};
 				cpu_crit0: trip1 {
@@ -2395,8 +2395,8 @@
 
 			trips {
 				cpu_alert1: trip0 {
-					temperature = <75000>;
-					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					temperature = <80000>;
+					hysteresis = <5000>;
 					type = "passive";
 				};
 				cpu_crit1: trip1 {
@@ -2422,8 +2422,8 @@
 
 			trips {
 				cpu_alert2: trip0 {
-					temperature = <75000>;
-					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					temperature = <80000>;
+					hysteresis = <5000>;
 					type = "passive";
 				};
 				cpu_crit2: trip1 {
@@ -2449,8 +2449,8 @@
 
